.TH GITFULL 1 "2026-09-21" "gitfull 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" Man page for gitfull. Kept in sync with src/main.rs usage() and the
.\" crate version by tests/packaging.rs. Installed by every distro package
.\" (see docs/PACKAGING.md).
.SH NAME
gitfull \- forge-agnostic package manager for Git-forge-hosted repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitfull
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitfull
treats any Git-forge-hosted repository as an installable package:
GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Codeberg, or any self-hosted forge.
Each install clones the repository into a per-app sandbox that gitfull
manages, provisions the toolchains the build needs (from source, with
the host compiler used exactly once, for the seed GCC), builds there,
and copies exactly one artifact out: the final binary, hashed and
audit-logged, into the configured bin directory.
.PP
A bare package name triggers ranked multi-forge search: every
configured forge is queried, candidates are scored by stars,
contributors, commit count, and recency, the ranked table and the
chosen repository are printed before anything is cloned or built, and
the top match is auto-selected.
.PP
No OS package manager is ever invoked by gitfull; every subprocess
spawn passes a single audited exec chokepoint.
.PP
All state-changing commands require root: run them as
.B "sudo gitfull install ...",
.B "sudo gitfull remove ...",
and so on. Read-only commands never do.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS State-changing (run as root)
.TP
.BI "install " "spec ..."
Install packages. Missing toolchain components are fetched and built
automatically.
.TP
.BI "update " "name ..."
Re-clone and rebuild installed packages; with no names, all installed
packages.
.TP
.BI "remove " "name ..."
Remove installed packages, verifying recorded hashes first.
.TP
.BI "toolchain bootstrap-gcc " "option..."
Optional manual seed-GCC build;
.B install
does this automatically when needed.
.TP
.BI "toolchain build " "component option..."
Optional manual toolchain component build.
.SS Read-only (no root required)
.TP
.B list
List installed packages.
.TP
.BI "info " query
Show the install record, or the ranked forge resolution for a bare
name.
.TP
.B toolchain\ list
Show the toolchain catalog and installed versions.
.TP
.B doctor
Environment readiness checks.
.TP
.B "config show | validate | path"
Inspect the configuration file.
.TP
.BI "audit " "N"
Show the last \fIN\fR audit events (default 20).
.SH PACKAGE SPECS
.TP
.I name
Ranked search across all configured forges; the resolution is printed
before anything happens.
.TP
.I forge:name
Ranked search scoped to one forge.
.TP
.I owner/repo
Default forge, no search.
.TP
.I forge:owner/repo
Explicit forge; bypasses ranking.
.TP
.IR owner/repo @ ref
Pinned branch, tag, or commit.
.TP
.I https://host/owner/repo.git
Full URL, matched against configured forges.
.TP
.I /abs/path
Local source tree (no network).
.SH OPTIONS
Global options precede the command:
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Configuration file (default \fI/etc/gitfull.conf\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-root " path"
Override the sandbox root.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve and plan only.
.TP
.B \-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y
Assume yes.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colors; \fB\-\-color auto|always|never\fR selects explicitly.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-v
Echo build commands.
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR, \fB\-V
Print the version. \fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-h\fR prints full help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 usage error; 3 policy or privilege violation; 4 build
failure; 5 package not installed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/gitfull.conf
Configuration. Never created or modified by gitfull or by the distro
packages; start from \fI/etc/gitfull.conf.example\fR.
.TP
.I /var/lib/gitfull
Sandbox root: per-app sandboxes, shared toolchains, cache, logs, and
the audit log. Created by gitfull on the first state-changing run, not
at package install time.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
sudo gitfull install meson
.RS
Ranked search across configured forges, then a sandboxed build with
automatic toolchain provisioning.
.RE
.PP
gitfull info meson
.RS
Show the ranked resolution read-only.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation ships in \fI/usr/share/doc/gitfull\fR (README,
ARCHITECTURE, AUDIT, CONFIG, PACKAGING).
